From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:10:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve resource URLs against the document's <base href>

Linked stylesheets, images (src, srcset and <picture> sources), iframes,
<style> sheets and style attributes resolved their URLs against the
document URL, so a page that keeps its assets in another folder through
<base href> loaded none of them, while baseURI on the JS side already
followed the base.

Keep url as the document URL and add document_base_url beside it: the
first <base href> in tree order, resolved against the document URL. A
data:, javascript: or vbscript: base, or one that does not parse or
cannot be a base, leaves the document URL; Chrome ignores data: and
javascript: bases. What means "this document" (the same-document check
for fragment links, the selector cache key) does not move with the base.

sync_base_url brings the base up to date before a fetch, a sheet parse
or a style attribute parse, and recomputes only after base_epoch moves.
The connected <base> elements are tracked as they connect and
disconnect, so a document with no <base href> never walks the tree, and
one with a single <base href> reads it directly. Only two or more need
the walk for tree order. Resources that already loaded are not fetched
again when the base changes, as in browsers.

Each <link rel=stylesheet> records the URL it was requested with
(linked_stylesheet_url), so an embedder can find the fetched sheet
after a later base change instead of resolving the href again.

Signed-off-by: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
